  "id": "communication-overload",
  "term": "communication overload",
  "definition": "Communication overload is a state in which a person has more verbal communication to take in during videoconferencing than they can comfortably process. In the source, it rises with more frequent videoconferencing and is linked to feeling overloaded with information and more fatigued by video meetings.",
